<title>INDONESIA: Indocement says Q1 earnings drop.</title>
<headline>Indocement says Q1 earnings drop.</headline>
<dateline>JAKARTA 1997-05-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Three months to March 31</p>
<p>				  (in billion rupiah unless stated)</p>
<p>    Net income		     89.17     vs   100.49</p>
<p>    Earnings per share (rph)     148     vs     166</p>
<p>    Net revenues		  1,103.24   vs   996.10</p>
<p>    Gross profit		    397.33   vs   369.30</p>
<p>    Income from operations	274.79   vs   253.36</p>
<p>    Charges			  (101.12)  vs   (83.89)</p>
<p>    Minority interests	    (50.41)  vs   (36.79)</p>
<p>Note: PT Indocement Tunggal Prakarsa, a member of the Salim Group, is one of the largest cement producers in Indonesia. The results were unaudited.</p>
</text>
